Project Title

Digital Canteen Ordering System

Problem Statement

In many schools, students face long queues and delays when buying food from the canteen. This not only wastes valuable time but can also cause stress and crowding, especially during peak lunch hours. Traditional manual ordering processes often result in inefficiency, errors, or insufficient monitoring of student spending.
This project seeks to address the problem by creating a digital canteen ordering system that allows students to order food without physically lining up, ensuring convenience, proper balance management, and faster service.

Project Objectives

To develop a system that enables students to order food digitally from the canteen.

To integrate a balance-checking mechanism that prevents transactions when funds are insufficient.

To provide a daily updated menu with corresponding prices.

To reduce long queues and improve overall efficiency in canteen transactions.

To create a simple, user-friendly system that can be easily accessed by students.

**Planned Features**

Student login with account balance.

Menu display with prices updated daily.

Ordering function with automatic balance deduction.

Restriction from ordering if balance is insufficient.

Confirmation system before finalizing the order.

Display of remaining balance after each purchase.

Planned Inputs and Outputs

Inputs:

Student name and account balance.

Food item selection from the menu.

Order confirmation (Yes/No).

Outputs:

Menu display with prices.

Notification if balance is insufficient.

Remaining balance after order.

Confirmation message that the order has been sent.
